<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter IV of Aragon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1319–<a href="/years/1387">1387</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Peter the Ceremonious · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-barcelona">House of Barcelona</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter IV, called the Ceremonious, was king of Aragon from 1336. He annexed the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a> in 1343-1344, fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> in the War of the Two Peters and suppressed the noble Unions. In 1379-1380 the Catalan duchies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ypati">Neopatras</a> accepted his rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-iv-of-aragon.jpg" alt="Peter IV of Aragon" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jaume Mateu (Before 1402 - After 1452) Born in Documented in Valencia. Details on Google Art Project · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jaume_Mateu_-_Peter_IV_the_Ceremonious_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Peter IV</b> fought the long War of the Two Peters against Castile from 1356 to 1369, in which Aragon suffered repeated invasions.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…France and the papacy over Sicily, nobles and towns organised in the Union of Aragon forced him to grant the General Privilege, and in 1287 Alfonso III yielded the still wider Privileges of the Union, until <b>Peter IV</b> crushed the Union at the Battle of Épila in 1348.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1359, at the Corts of Cervera, <b>Peter IV</b> accepted a standing committee to collect the taxes voted by the Corts, the Diputació del General, later called the Generalitat, which grew into a powerful body defending the Principality’s constitutions.</blockquote><a href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Principality of Catalonia · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1379-1380 the duchies passed to <b>Peter IV of Aragon</b>, who called the Acropolis the most beautiful jewel in the world.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-neopatras">Duchy of Neopatras</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Peter IV of Aragon</b> seized the kingdom in 1343-1344, and James III was killed at Llucmajor in 1349 trying to retake it.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-majorca">Kingdom of Majorca</a></li></ul></section>
